                <h3 id="AN5.210" class="h1">Muddled Mindfulness<br/>
                  Muṭṭhassati Sutta  (AN 5:210)</h3><!--end suttahead-->
<p>“Monks, there are these five drawbacks for one who falls asleep unalert &amp; with muddled mindfulness. Which five?</p>
<p>“One sleeps badly, wakes up badly, dreams evil dreams. The devas don’t protect one. Semen is emitted.</p>
<p>“These, monks, are the five drawbacks for one who falls asleep unalert &amp; with muddled mindfulness.</p>
<p>“There are these five rewards for one who falls asleep alert &amp; with mindfulness established. Which five?</p>
<p>“One sleeps easily, wakes up easily, dreams no evil dreams. The devas protect one. Semen is not emitted.</p>
<p>“These, monks, are the five rewards for one who falls asleep alert &amp; with mindfulness established.”</p>
<p class="seealso">See also: <a href="AN5_56.html">AN 5:56</a>; <a href="AN6_17.html">AN 6:17</a>; <a href="AN11_16.html">AN 11:16</a>; <a href="../KN/Dhp/Ch02.html#dhp029">Dhp 29</a>; <a href="../KN/Dhp/Ch23.html#dhp325">Dhp 325</a>; <a href="../KN/StNp/StNp2_10.html">Sn 2:10</a>; <a href="../KN/Thag/thag1_84.html">Thag 1:84</a>; <a href="../KN/Thag/thag2_37.html">Thag 2:37</a></p>
      </div><!--end:sutta-->
